    body: `Mass m<sub>${spec.i}</sub> sits at the cube corner ${plain}, with coordinates written in units of the edge length a. It belongs to the ${groupTxt}. Because ions alternate along every edge, none of its three nearest corner neighbours has the same colour. Feeding all eight positions into R = (\u03A3 m\u1D62 r\u1D62)/(\u03A3 m\u1D62) gives the centre of mass of the cell \u2014 (a/2, a/2, a/2) when the eight masses are equal.`
